.TH HD-AUDACIOUS 7 "October 2026" "hd-audacious" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-audacious \- the audio player audacious with a terminal interface
.SH DESCRIPTION
The package
.B hd-audacious
holds the audio player
.BR audacious (1)
with a terminal interface, from the forks of audacious and audacious-plugins
of HyprDebian. It replaces the packages
.BR audacious ,
.B audacious-plugins
and
.B audacious-plugins-data
of Debian.
.PP
.PP
It is built for a small footprint, without GTK, Qt or any other graphical
library, with only the plugins for the terminal interface, MPRIS, FLAC, MP3
and WAV, the output to PipeWire and the playlist files m3u, pls and audpl.
ReplayGain is part of audacious itself and on by default, in track mode; it
reads the tags of FLAC files and the ID3v2 and APE tags of MP3 files.
.PP
.B /usr/bin/audacious
starts the binary in
.I /usr/lib/hd-audacious/bin
with
.BR \-\-tui .
All arguments are handed on to it unchanged. Started from a terminal,
audacious runs in it. Started without one, as from the application launcher
or an opener of yazi, it hands its command line to the instance of
audacious that runs, as audacious does over D-Bus; when that instance does
not run, it starts in a new kitty window of the class
.BR audacious .
The package only recommends kitty, so that it pulls in no graphical
libraries; without kitty, audacious only starts from a terminal.
With
.BR \-\-headless ,
.B \-\-help
or
.B \-\-version
it runs without the terminal interface.
.PP
The output of audacious goes to
.I /tmp/audacious-tui-<user>.log
while the terminal interface runs, so that it does not mix with the
interface.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Up, Down, Page Up, Page Down
Move through the playlist.
.TP
.B Enter
Play the song in the playlist.
.TP
.B Space
Pause or play.
.TP
.B Left, Right
Seek 5 seconds back or forward.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH REMOTE CONTROL
The plugin mpris2, which is enabled from the start, lets the media keys of
the desktop control audacious with
.BR playerctl (1).
.BR audtool (1)
controls it from a shell:
.PP
.nf
audtool playlist-addurl ~/Music/album
audtool playback-play
.fi
.SH SETTINGS
The terminal interface has no settings window. The settings are in
.IR ~/.config/audacious/config ,
which audacious writes when it quits, so change it while audacious does not
run. ReplayGain is in the section
.BR [audacious] :
.TP
.B enable_replay_gain
TRUE or FALSE; TRUE by default.
.TP
.B replay_gain_mode
0 for track gain, the default, 1 for album gain, 2 for album gain, but track
gain while the playlist is shuffled.
.TP
.B replay_gain_preamp
The gain to add, in dB; 0 by default.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/audacious
Starts audacious with its terminal interface.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/hd-audacious
The binaries, the private libraries libaudcore and libaudtag, and the
plugins in
.IR audacious/ .
.TP
.I ~/.config/audacious
The settings and playlists of a user.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR audacious (1),
.BR audtool (1),
.BR hd-desktop (7),
.BR hd-yazi (1)
